A||N||7||TSPalmer||What kind of price should I offer?||||5||
Z||000000||TSPalmer||09-19-2001||03:13 PM||||Hey everyone.  There is a guy in our neighborhood that has a black aero coupe that I've been wanting for some time now.  I had talked to him about it a few months ago (it's been sitting quite a while) and he said that it had a blown engine and that his son was planning on getting a new engine for it and didn't want to sell it.  I see it every day on the way to work, rotting away. <P>Anyway, he came over to my house Saturday as I was leaving to get the family some dinner and said that his son decided not to rebuild and if I wanted it to make him an offer.  <P>Therein lies my delima.  I know this much about the car (he wasn't there when I did get the chance to look it over): blown V6, not sure of the year but it's got the aero nose and 3rd brake light (would make it an 86, 87 or 88), nothing on the sail panels, nothing on the trunk stickerwise, the front fascia is cracked where the Fiero emblem is on my 85 SE (ie. no Fiero emblem on the nose), pw, pdl, paint is so-so for a car with an inspection sticker that expired 10/99, interior is salvageable, steering wheel is missing horn buttons, missing battery cover, luggage rack with missing paint.<P>I was thinking of getting it for the panels and the power goodies.  I know it's not much to go on, but I was wondering if you kind folks could give me an idea on what to offer the guy.  I'm not sure of the mileage, but I'm not that worried about it anyway as this would be a parts car for me.<P>Thanks for any ideas,<BR>Shawn<P>BTW: couldn't really tell if it had a 5spd or a 4spd, but it's a manual shift.<P>(Edited for manual transmission omission...LOL   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<BR>------------------<BR>T.Shawn Palmer<BR>'85 SE 4cyl 5spd<p>[This message has been edited by TSPalmer (edited 09-19-2001).]||||reg||5
